lay="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−3</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−3</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span>: (a) an electron and (b) a bowling ball of mass 6.0 kg.
<p id="fs-id1170901922139"></p><h4 data-type="title">Strategy</h4>
Given the uncertainty in speed <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−3</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−3</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span>, we have to first determine the uncertainty in momentum <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mtext> </mtext><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mtext> </mtext><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>u</mi></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> and then invert <a href="7-2-the-heisenberg-uncertainty-principle#fs-id1170901907603" class="autogenerated-content" aria-label="Go to Equation 7.15">Equation 7.15</a> to find the uncertainty in position <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℏ</mi><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mrow><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℏ</mi><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span>.
<p id="fs-id1170902908721"></p><h4 data-type="title">Solution</h4>
<ol id="fs-id1170901627145" type="a">
<li>For the electron:
<div data-type="equation" id="fs-id1170901766421" class="unnumbered" data-label=""><math display="block"><semantics><mrow><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign="right"><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>p</mi></mtd><mtd columnalign="left"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd columnalign="left"><mi>m</mi><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>9.1</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>−31</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>−3</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>m/s</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>9.1</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>−34</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>·</mo><mtext>m/s</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mo>,</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign="right"><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>x</mi></mtd><mtd columnalign="left"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd columnalign="left"><mfrac><mi>ℏ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mtext> </mtext><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5.8</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext><mtext>.</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign="right"><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>p</mi></mtd><mtd columnalign="left"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd columnalign="left"><mi>m</mi><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>9.1</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>−31</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>−3</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>m/s</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>9.1</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>−34</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>·</mo><mtext>m/s</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mo>,</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign="right"><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>x</mi></mtd><mtd columnalign="left"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd columnalign="left"><mfrac><mi>ℏ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mtext> </mtext><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5.8</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext><mtext>.</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></annotation-xml></semantics></math></div></li>
<li>For the bowling ball:
<div data-type="equation" id="fs-id1170902918463" class="unnumbered" data-label=""><math display="block"><semantics><mrow><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign="right"><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>p</mi></mtd><mtd columnalign="left"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd columnalign="left"><mi>m</mi><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6.0</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>−3</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>m/s</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>6.0</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>−3</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>·</mo><mtext>m/s</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mo>,</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign="right"><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>x</mi></mtd><mtd columnalign="left"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd columnalign="left"><mfrac><mi>ℏ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mtext> </mtext><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>8.8</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>−33</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>m</mtext><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mtext>.</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign="right"><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>p</mi></mtd><mtd columnalign="left"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd columnalign="left"><mi>m</mi><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6.0</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>−3</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>m/s</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>6.0</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>−3</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>·</mo><mtext>m/s</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mo>,</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign="right"><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>x</mi></mtd><mtd columnalign="left"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd columnalign="left"><mfrac><mi>ℏ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mtext> </mtext><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>8.8</mn><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>−33</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>m</mtext><mspace width="0.2em"></mspace><mtext>.</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></annotation-xml></semantics></math></div></li>
</ol>
<p id="fs-id1170901501570"></p><h4 data-type="title">Significance</h4>
Unlike the position uncertainty for the electron, the position uncertainty for the bowling ball is immeasurably small. Planck’s constant is very small, so the limitations imposed by the uncertainty principle are not noticeable in macr